WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/notifications/components/BrowserPushChannelCard.tsx — the per-device browser/OS push
  channel settings card. GlassPanel → header[ cyan icon chip (BellRing) + h3 "Browser push" + subtitle ]
  + status Badge(success "Active on this device" / neutral "Not subscribed" / warning "Unavailable").
  Body branch: isUnsupported ? amber AlertCircle callout(disabledReason) : Enable/Disable button + iOS note.
  Then the "Registered devices" list (rows.length>0): per row a Smartphone icon, user_agent (or "Unknown
  browser"), "(this device)" when currentEndpoint===row.endpoint, "Last used {formatRelative}"/"Not yet used",
  and a Trash2 revoke button.
  disabledReason IIFE (four-way, first match wins):
    !notifSupported                                   → webpush.unsupported.notification
    !isPushSupported && !keyLoading && publicKey===null→ webpush.unsupported.serverDisabled
    !isPushSupported                                  → webpush.unsupported.pushApi
    permission==='denied'                             → webpush.unsupported.permissionDenied
  Six data hooks: useTranslation, useWebPush, usePushPublicKey, usePushSubscriptions, useUnsubscribePush
  (the `usePush` api-hooks file).

